Package: tides
Title: Truncation-Induced Dependency Among Summary Statistics
Version: 0.3.2
Authors@R:
    person("Ian", "Hussey", , "ian.hussey@unibe.ch", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8906-7559"))
Description: Forensic meta-science tools for checking reported summary
    statistics measured on a bounded (truncated) scale. When a measure has a
    known minimum and maximum, the reported mean constrains the standard
    deviation that is arithmetically possible, so the two are not independent.
    The package computes the smallest and largest standard deviations that a
    reported mean, sample size and scale range could have produced and flags
    reports that fall outside those bounds as inconsistent. The idea extends
    granularity-based consistency checks such as GRIM and GRIMMER (Brown and
    Heathers (2017) <doi:10.1177/1948550616673876>) to the dispersion of
    truncated data. Helpers apply the check across a data frame, visualise the
    feasible envelope of means and standard deviations, and enumerate the grid
    of jointly GRIM-, GRIMMER- and truncation-consistent values.
